<Styles xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        xmlns:mf="using:MonkeyForged.Design.Avalonia">
  <!--
    Rules more than one area uses: the locked button, the switch, the small button and the tag. Included
    first, so an area can override a rule of this file in its own file (plan s13.1, I-3).

    Under the design package's theme (story s13.1) a Button gets the package's face: a
    chamfered border that draws the button's own Background, BorderBrush and Foreground. A
    rule colours a real button on the button itself, its states included
    (Button.x:pointerover); "/template/ ContentPresenter" reaches only the bare buttons
    (Theme/Bare.axaml), whose presenter is the face. The face draws its frame as the whole
    polygon and the fill inset on top, so a real button never gets a transparent Background:
    the frame colour would fill it. An outline button keeps the package's own fill.
  -->

  <!--
    A locked button is the package's locked look, whatever an area sets on it: flat
    bg-overlay without a frame, ink-faint text. The rule hits the face in the package's
    template, which beats every setter on the button — the forge start and the signal stop
    included, so a locked start button stays grey while the game runs (test ActionColorTests).
  -->
  <Style Selector="Button:disabled /template/ mf|ChamferBorder#PART_Face">
    <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource BgOverlayBrush}" />
    <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{x:Null}" />
  </Style>
  <Style Selector="Button:disabled /template/ mf|ChamferBorder#PART_Face > ContentPresenter">
    <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource InkFaintBrush}" />
  </Style>

  <!--
    The switch is the package's ToggleSwitch, states and colours included, as its track alone:
    the label of a switch row stands in the row. Fluent's On/Off labels and its minimum width
    are taken back, and the width is the track's 40 — the template keeps a 12 px column after
    the track for a label even without one, which pushed the track away from the edge it
    belongs to (Settings, Modules) or the status line away from it (bridge card).
  -->
  <Style Selector="ToggleSwitch.switch">
    <Setter Property="OnContent" Value="{x:Null}" />
    <Setter Property="OffContent" Value="{x:Null}" />
    <Setter Property="MinWidth" Value="0" />
    <Setter Property="Width" Value="40" />
  </Style>

  <!--
    The small button, a quiet frame in ink-muted that lights forge under the pointer: the folder
    actions of the right column, Rescan, the empty state's action, the buttons of the Settings
    rows and of the log page. An area that wants another tone sets it in its own file.
  -->
  <Style Selector="Button.small">
    <Setter Property="Padding" Value="12,6" />
    <Setter Property="MinHeight" Value="0" />
    <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1" />
    <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{StaticResource LineStrongBrush}" />
    <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource InkMutedBrush}" />
    <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="12" />
  </Style>
  <Style Selector="Button.small:pointerover">
    <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{StaticResource ForgeBrush}" />
    <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ForgeHotBrush}" />
  </Style>

  <!--
    Every tag reads in the package's label font. The package draws a tag in the pixel font
    Silkscreen at 10 px, which sits on 1.25 screen pixels per font pixel and blurs ("CE" reads
    like "OE"). The tag's template follows the control's own font properties, so these three
    setters reach its text; colour, frame, dot, height and capitals stay the package's. The size
    is the package's own tag size (TextPixelFontSize, 10 px) rather than the label size (12 px):
    the owner found 12 px too large (spec s15.5). The letter spacing is left alone on purpose
    (spec s15.4).
  -->
  <Style Selector="mf|Tag">
    <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{StaticResource TextLabelFontFamily}" />
    <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="{StaticResource TextPixelFontSize}" />
    <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="{StaticResource TextLabelFontWeight}" />
  </Style>
</Styles>
